.TH HSYNC-BOOTNODE 1 "2026-09-30" "hsync-bootnode 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hsync-bootnode \- HSYNC P2P bootstrap node (no-log, in-memory, zero-knowledge)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsync-bootnode
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B hsync-bootnode --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsync-bootnode
is the Internet discovery node of the HSYNC sync network. It tells P2P clients
which peers are currently online, speaking the
.B boot/1
protocol over QUIC/UDP port 443 (TLS 1.3 inside QUIC, mandatory RETRY and
address-validation tokens).
.PP
The routing table lives exclusively in RAM with a configurable TTL (default
60 seconds, 1\-3600): nothing peer-related is ever written to disk, no log file
is produced, and the TLS identity is generated per process unless the operator
opts into persistence with
.BR "run \-\-identity" .
Stopping the process erases every trace of the network.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the bootstrap node: single QUIC/UDP listener (boot/1).
.TP
.B identity show
Print the persisted identity fingerprint (or its certificate PEM with
.BR \-\-pem ).
.TP
.B identity rotate
Regenerate the persisted identity and print the new fingerprint.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--host\fP= HOST
Address to bind the QUIC/UDP listener to. Accepts an optional port
.RI ( HOST [: PORT ],
e.g.
.IR 0.0.0.0:443
or
.IR [::1]:443 ).
Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--port\fP= PORT
UDP port (1\-65535). Default: 443 (QUIC/HTTP3). Ports below 1024 need root or
.BR CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE .
Mutually exclusive with a port in
.BR \-\-host .
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--identity\fP= PATH
Persist the TLS identity (key+cert) at
.I PATH
so the certificate fingerprint is stable across restarts and can be pinned by
clients. Without it the identity stays in-memory (ephemeral default). The file
is written with 0600 permissions in a 0700 directory and contains no peer data.
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--public-host\fP= NAME
Public hostname or IP to add to the certificate SAN; repeatable for multiple
names.
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--protected-bucket\fP= NAME
Bucket requiring a valid
.I bucket_token
Repeatable for multiple buckets. Declaring a protected bucket without
provisioning its key fails fast at startup with exit code 2.
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--keys-fd\fP= FD
File descriptor carrying the group keys, one
.I bucket=<hex\-key>
line per group; blank lines and
.I #
comments are ignored. Read once at startup, never written to disk.
.TP
.B run\ \fR--private\fP
Private node: every frame must carry a valid
.I bucket_token
(applied to the whole node, not only to the buckets declared with
.BR \-\-protected\-bucket ).
A bucket without a group key is refused exactly like a wrong token, and
.I leave
is gated too (an unauthenticated leave is silently dropped). Starting a private
node with no group key fails fast with exit code 2. Env form:
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_PRIVATE=1 .
.TP
.B run\ \fR--no-upnp\fP
Disable the zero-touch UPnP UDP port mapping.
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--ttl\fP= SECONDS
Record TTL in seconds (1\-3600). Default: 60 (peers refresh every 30 s).
.TP
.B run\ \fR--debug\fP
Emit the full operation log to stderr (opt\-in; off by default): connections,
frames, decisions, record changes and TTL sweeps, including the peer identity
(CID, bucket, IP, port) needed for analysis. Stderr only \- it is never
written to disk, and without it no peer data leaves memory. Env form:
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_DEBUG=1 .
.TP
.BI run\ \fR--ready-file\fP= PATH
Write the process PID to
.I PATH
once the QUIC listener is bound, and remove it on graceful shutdown (contains
no peer data). Env form:
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_READY_FILE .
.TP
.B run\ \fR--no-rate-limit\fP
Disable rate limiting entirely (benchmark/test seam; never in production — it
removes the anti\-abuse limits the spec requires). Env form:
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_NO_RATE_LIMIT=1 .
.TP
.B \fR--version\fP
Print the version and the protocol, then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_KEYS_FD
Integer file descriptor carrying the group keys; same as
.BR "run \-\-keys\-fd" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_DEBUG
Set to
.I 1
to enable the full operation log on stderr (peer identity included); same as
.BR "run \-\-debug" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_READY_FILE
Path for the readiness PID file; same as
.BR "run \-\-ready\-file" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_NO_RATE_LIMIT
Set to
.I 1
to disable rate limiting (benchmark/test seam); same as
.BR "run \-\-no\-rate\-limit" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_PRIVATE
Set to
.I 1
to require a valid
.I bucket_token
on every frame (private node); same as
.BR "run \-\-private" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_VERSION
Overrides the version used by
.BR compile.sh (1)
when building executables and packages (per-language binaries live in
e.g. python/compile.sh).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hsync-bootnode/group-keys
Group keys for protected buckets, one
.I bucket=<hex\-key>
per line. Provisioned by the administrator (never part of the package;
created by postinst as a root-only 0750 directory); exposed to the service
only through the systemd credential mechanism (see
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_KEYS_FD ).
.TP
.I /var/lib/hsync-bootnode/identity.pem
Example opt-in path for the persistent TLS identity (certificate + private
key, 0600), created by
.BR "run \-\-identity" ;
contains no peer data. Rotate it with
.BR "identity rotate" .
.B \-\-identity
accepts any writable path: with the packaged unit's DynamicUser sandbox the
node cannot persist it itself, so provision the file out of band or relax the
sandbox with an override.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hsync-bootnode.service
Hardened systemd unit (DynamicUser, ProtectSystem=strict, SystemCallFilter,
StandardOutput=null). Installed but not enabled: opt in with
.B systemctl enable --now hsync-bootnode.service.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hsync-bootnode
Standalone executable (symlink to
.IR /usr/lib/hsync-bootnode/hsync-bootnode ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open mode (no protected buckets):
.B hsync-bootnode run --host 0.0.0.0 --port 443
.TP
Protected bucket with keys from a file descriptor:
.br
.B hsync-bootnode run --protected-bucket shared --keys-fd 5 5</etc/hsync-bootnode/group-keys
.TP
Private node (every bucket needs a key; no anonymous frames):
.br
.B hsync-bootnode run --private --keys-fd 5 5</etc/hsync-bootnode/group-keys
.TP
Show the certificate fingerprint printed at startup to pin the node on
clients:
.br
.B hsync-bootnode run --port 443
.TP
Run with a persistent identity so the fingerprint is stable across restarts,
then read the fingerprint to distribute to clients:
.br
.B hsync-bootnode run --identity /var/lib/hsync-bootnode/identity.pem --public-host boot.example.com
.br
.B hsync-bootnode identity show --identity /var/lib/hsync-bootnode/identity.pem
.TP
Rotate the identity after a suspected compromise:
.br
.B hsync-bootnode identity rotate --identity /var/lib/hsync-bootnode/identity.pem
.TP
Unprivileged port (no root or capability needed):
.br
.B hsync-bootnode run --port 8443
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination (Ctrl+C or SIGTERM).
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error (missing/duplicate group key, private node without a key,
out-of-range value): the node refuses to start.
.TP
.B 3
Listener bind failure: the QUIC/UDP port is privileged, already in use, or
.B --host
is not a local address. The message on stderr explains the remediation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
